      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.1",
      "title": "Historical sources and datation",
      "body": "● Miniatures sometimes display a small shield attached to the aventail, mainly during the 14th century. Those shields were supposed to show the heraldry of the wearer. Thus, as neck protection is mandatory in our sport, such neck shields can be allowed to be worn on the aventail.\n● They are approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nBook of Hours - 1320 - The Netherlands",
